  "original_context": {
    "full_target": "Let n,m be integer dimensions with n,m≥1, let u:ℝ^n×(0,∞)→ℝ^m be jointly smooth, and fix q∈ℝ^m with |q|=1. Assume |u(x,t)|=1 everywhere; at every (x,t) there exists a real a with u_tt(x,t)−Δ_xu(x,t)=a u(x,t), with no regularity of a assumed; and for every 0<s<t<∞ there is a compact C_[s,t]⊂ℝ^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_[s,t] and r∈[s,t]. Spatial compact support means this locally uniform compact support of the perturbation u−q, not compact support of u itself. With Euclidean norms, Frobenius spatial gradient square, componentwise Laplacian and Lebesgue measure, put e(x,t)=|u_t(x,t)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,t)|² and E(t)=∫_{ℝ^n}e(x,t) dx. Prove integrability of every spatial section of e, differentiability of E on (0,∞), and E'(t)=0 for every t>0; consequently E is constant there. There is no assertion at time zero.",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "id": "H001",
        "statement": "n≥1 and m≥1.",
        "origin": "problem.md:25"
      },
      {
        "id": "H002",
