        "statement": "|q|=1.",
        "origin": "problem.md:27"
      },
      {
        "id": "H004",
        "statement": "For every x∈ℝ^n and t>0, |u(x,t)|=1.",
        "origin": "problem.md:29"
      },
      {
        "id": "H005",
        "statement": "For every x∈ℝ^n and t>0 there exists a real scalar a such that u_tt(x,t)−Δ_xu(x,t)=a u(x,t). No regularity of a selection of these scalars is assumed.",
        "origin": "problem.md:30-33"
      },
      {
        "id": "H006",
        "statement": "For every pair of real times 0<s<t<∞ there is a compact set C_[s,t]⊂ℝ^n such that for every x∉C_[s,t] and every r∈[s,t], u(x,r)=q.",
        "origin": "problem.md:34-36"
      }
    ],
    "conclusion": "For every t>0, e(·,t) is Lebesgue integrable on ℝ^n. The finite integral E is differentiable on (0,∞), and for every t>0, E'(t)=0. For every s,t>0, E(s)=E(t)."
